    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I need help writing a rejection email. We had a candidate, Marcus, who made it all the way to the final interview for our Senior Dev role here in Austin. He's really talented and had great technical skills, but we decided to go with someone who had a bit more experience with our specific cloud architecture. I want the email to be professional and kind because he was a great guy, but we need to be firm that the decision is final. Can you draft something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft rejection email that balances professionalism with kindness, while also acknowledging the importance of being firm:\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior Developer position at our Austin office. We were truly impressed by your technical skills and the enthusiasm you brought to our final interview. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience aligns more closely with our specific cloud architecture needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the prospect of having you join our team. Your passion for development and commitment to excellence are traits that we value highly, and we have no doubt that you will find a role that is a great fit for your skills and experience.\n\nI want to emphasize that this decision is final, and we appreciate the time and effort you invested in our interview process. We're confident that you will find a new opportunity that will allow you to grow and thrive in your career, just as a skilled craftsman might find a new project that showcases their unique talents.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out. We wish you all the best in your future endeavors and hope that our paths will cross again soon.\n\nBest",
