    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft:\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior Developer position at our Austin office. We were truly impressed by your technical skills and the enthusiasm you brought to our final interview. Your passion for development and commitment to excellence are traits that we value highly, and we were excited to see how you would fit in with our team.\n\nAs we weighed the various factors in our decision, we realized that we're looking for a candidate who can not only hit the ground running, but also help us drive our cloud architecture forward in the next 6-12 months. While your experience and skills are a great match for many aspects of the role, we felt that the pace of our growth and the complexity of our current projects might be a bit too steep for you to tackle right away.\n\nPlease know that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a developer. We were genuinely impressed by your work and would love to have you join our team in the future. In fact, we'd like to keep your resume on file for any future openings that might be a better fit for your skills and experience. We're always on the lookout for talented individuals like you, and we're confident that",
